Alert Box
	This is a message alerting you to a problem.
	
	If it is a Question Dialog (shown by the question 
	mark icon), then a response from you is required.
	Click on the `Yes' or `No' to respond to the
	question.
	
	Otherwise, click the `OK' button to acknowledge the
	message and close the box.
File Selector
	Click in the list of `Files' on the right to select
	a file (copy the file pathname to the 'Selection' field).
	 Double-click in the list of `Directories' on the
	left to change to another directory. Double-click on the
	double dot (..) to climb the directory tree.
	 You can change the files `Filter' field using
	standard shell regular expression characters and
	click in the `Filter' button to filter the current
	directory. Changing the filter to an asterisk will
	show all the files in the directory.
	 To validate your choice, which is shown in the
	`Selection' field, click on the `OK' button,
	or double-click on the selected file name in the
	Files list.
	 To cancel the selection, and any changes you may
	have made, click on `Cancel'.
	See the OSF/Motif Style Guide for more information
	on using the Motif File Selector.
Template Name
	Choose the name of a template in the list.
	This template will be applied (or un-applied)
	to the specified widget(s).
Restart Design Process
	The XFaceMaker design process has terminated.
	 XFaceMaker will now launch a new one by executing the
	command line contained in the text field of this dialog
	box.
	
	 Click `OK' to launch the command. Type `Cancel' to
	not launch any command (an alert box will warn you that
	you are now running without any design process).
	
	 If you click the `Wait' button, XFaceMaker will not
	launch any process. Instead, it will wait for an external
	design process to connect to it (for example, a design
	process launched by Gester).
	
	 You can edit the command line directly, or use the
	buttons below it.
	
	 The `Command...' push button will
	pop a file selector with which you can choose a
	different executable (for example an instance of xfm
	that you have created yourself using the FmCallEditor
	function).
	
	 The `Restore state' toggle adds or removes the option
	`-restore' in the command line: when this option is set,
	XFaceMaker will restore the state of the design process
	as when it terminated.
	
	 The `Trusted state' toggle adds or removes the option
	`-trusted', which will restore the state of the design
	process as when it was last automatically saved, which
	occurs every 30 seconds or when switching to Try mode.
	This option is useful when the design process encounters
	an error while re-building objects (for example if an
	xfmCreateCallback contains an execution error).
